---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects | Evan Hobson"
  description="Side projects: Game of Life ash statistics and a scripture text-analysis script."
>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Projects</h1>
    <p class="intro">Things I built outside of lab work. The code for both is on GitHub.</p>

    <div class="list">
      <article class="item">
        <h2>Game of Life ash</h2>
        <p class="meta">Python · 2026 · <a href="https://github.com/broncomcbuck/gol-ash-project">repository</a></p>
        <p>
          In Conway's Game of Life, a random starting grid (a "soup") eventually settles into stable
          and repeating objects called ash. Catagolue has counted ash from hundreds of trillions of
          soups, but always at 16×16 cells and 50% density. I varied soup size from 8 to 64 cells and
          density from 0.1 to 0.9 and described the ash with the same tools ecologists use for
          species counts: richness, Shannon entropy and rank-abundance curves.
        </p>
        <p>
          Across all 63 size and density combinations, Shannon entropy moved by only 0.04 bits, and
          time to stabilize grew with the side length of the grid rather than its area. A 630,000-soup
          rerun corrected a boundary bug that had inflated the share of soups that never settle.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="item">
        <h2>Emotion attributed to God in the Book of Mormon</h2>
        <p class="meta">Python · <a href="https://github.com/broncomcbuck/bomproject">repository</a></p>
        <p>
          A script that finds verses where an emotion is attributed to God, not just verses where
          "God" and an emotion word both appear. It matches on attribution patterns ("God's wrath",
          a God term followed by an emotion term) instead of word proximity. It has no model of
          negation or reported speech, so its output is a list of verses to read, not a measurement.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
